<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI3152-M5-WINDOWS-BUILD-BREAK>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI3152-M5-WINDOWS-BUILD-BREAK" ;
  triage:title "M5-ADMISSION-FIX-3 breaks the Windows build: unresolved crate::local_ipc_transport import on windows" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs:20 now imports `crate::local_ipc_transport::admission::{...}` (added by the M5-ADMISSION-FIX-3 join-deadline change). But crates/atm-daemon/src/lib.rs:28-29 gates the entire local_ipc_transport module behind `#[cfg(not(windows))]`. This produces a hard compile error (E0433: failed to resolve, could not find `local_ipc_transport` in the crate root) on windows-latest, confirmed via CI job logs for PR #722 run 30766398824. This directly contradicts arch-ctm's QA-3 claim that `just lint` and `just test` pass." ;
